      "role": "user",
      "content": "one thing is that 0.06 isn't \"significant\" in a grant review—the reviewers are gonna kill us if we present it that way. we need to frame the findings so they don't just reject the whole thing immediately. how can we word the results section to emphasize the trend without making it look like we're trying to hide the p-value?",
